 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block C (housekeeping, data-terms audit, W3 macro inputs, W12 assumptions)
+- `.gitignore`: `data/raw/**` is ignored except `SOURCES.csv`, READMEs and the World Bank snapshots; `.pytest_cache/` added. `git check-ignore` confirms the FinScope, ILFS, census and MoF raw files are ignored. Nothing was untracked or committed.
+- `docs/data_terms.md` (new): obligations, what is published, how third parties obtain each raw file. `data/raw/SOURCES.csv` gains a `citation` column (exact catalogue text) and the four WDI snapshots (CC BY 4.0, redistributable).
+- `run_all.py --fetch` (new): the only network call; `src/01_ingest/fetch_worldbank.py` saves the raw WDI responses unchanged to `data/raw/worldbank/<indicator>_<date>.json` and appends URL, time and SHA-256 to `MANIFEST.csv`. Without `--fetch` no network access happens; snapshots are named in `config.yaml worldbank.snapshots`.
+- New `src/03_features/macro_inputs.py` -> `outputs/stats/macro_inputs.json`: Tanzania tax-to-GDP 2024 (12.26%), benchmark = peer average of GHA, KEN, RWA, UGA in 2023 (13.12%, the latest year all five report), gap = (benchmark - Tanzania, same year) x GDP in TZS of that year = TZS 2.72 trillion (was the typed 7.29). `config.yaml macro.benchmark_source` (peer_average | cited_target); no citable target adopted.
+- `economic_model.py` reads GDP, tax-to-GDP, benchmark and exchange rate from `macro_inputs.json` (the typed 78.84B, 0.128, 0.165, 2,500 are gone): the twin, scenarios, property and mobile-money blocks change (list in BLOCK_C_REPORT.md).
+- New `config.yaml assumptions:` block (162 constants: DATA 13, ASSUMPTION 60, UNKNOWN 89) read through `src/assumptions.py`; values unchanged (outputs byte-identical to the pre-refactor run apart from the macro change). `assumption_ledger.py` writes `outputs/stats/assumption_ledger.json` from it with stable ids (`ASS-` + SHA-1 of the key). `src/tools/assumption_sensitivity.py` (+/-20%, 5% threshold) -> `docs/assumption_sensitivity.json`; `src/tools/build_assumptions_register.py` -> `docs/assumptions_register.csv` (with an empty `john_signoff` column) and `docs/model_internals.csv`.
+- `economic_model.json` `tax_morale_model.naive_sum_of_solo_effects_pct` = 78.004 (Fig 5.1 naive sum from unrounded values); 77.8 appears only when rebuilt from rounded probabilities.
+- Claims map: `block_c_decision` (Block B decisions) and `block_c_*` columns; 27 claims fed by UNKNOWN constants are marked BLOCKED.
+- New tests: `test_macro.py`, `test_assumptions.py`. `finscope_targeting_population_loader.py` reads the same assumptions as the model.
 
 ## 2026-11-11 - Phase 4, Block B (data-derived numbers: W5, W2, W4, W1)
 - New `src/03_features/tin_by_segment.py` (+ `survey_design.py`): TIN rate overall and for the five adult stages from one stratification and one weight, design-based 95% CIs (reconstructed design), reconciliation check that fails loudly -> `outputs/tables/tin_by_segment.csv`, `outputs/stats/tin_reconciliation.json`.
