+# Data terms: what we may do with the raw data, what is published, how others get it
+
+Written 2026-11-12 (Block C0.4). Sources of the wording: the catalogue pages read on 2026-11-11/12 (NBS microdata portal entries 63 and 45; fsdt.or.tz; mof.go.tz) and the terms as stated for this project. Exact catalogue texts and URLs are in `data/raw/SOURCES.csv` (columns `licence/terms`, `citation`, `redistributable`).
+
+## 1. Obligations (NBS and FSDT terms, identical in substance)
+
+1. **No redistribution of the raw data.** The respondent- or person-level files are not copied to anyone else, published, sold or placed in a public repository. NBS catalogue text: the data and other material "will not be redistributed or sold to other individuals, institutions, or organization without the written agreement of the Tanzania National Bureau of Statistics."
+2. **Aggregated reporting only.** Published results are aggregates (counts, rates, tables); no row-level records, no per-person scores derived row by row from real respondents.
+3. **No re-identification** of respondents, and **no record linkage** that could identify individuals (including by combining small cells or fine geography).
+4. **Cite each dataset as its catalogue requires** (section 3). NBS adds that users acknowledge NBS as the original collector of the data.
+5. **Send an electronic copy of every publication** that uses the data to the data owner (NBS; FSDT). *Not found in the catalogue pages and FSDT pages read; it is recorded here as stated for this project, to be checked against the signed confidentiality declaration / FSDT agreement.* Contacts printed in the sources: NBS Statistician General, sg@nbs.go.tz (ILFS 2020/21 report); FSDT, info@fsdt.or.tz (fsdt.or.tz).
+
+## 2. Status of each raw file
+
+| File | Owner | Redistribute raw? | How a third party obtains it |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `finscope/FinScope.csv`, `FinScope Datamap.xlsx` | FSDT (with NBS approval) | **unclear, treated as no** (no policy text found) | request form on https://www.fsdt.or.tz/finscope/ ("Download the Finscope Tanzania 2023 Datasets": name, organisation, e-mail) |
+| `ilfs/ILFS2024-URT-FINAL - Anonymized.sav` | NBS | **no** | free account on the NBS microdata portal, accept the confidentiality declaration, https://microdata.nbs.go.tz/index.php/catalog/63 |
+| `census/TPHC2022_TenPercent_DEMOGRAPHICS.sav` | NBS | **no** | same portal, https://microdata.nbs.go.tz/index.php/catalog/45 (the page does not name a 10% sample file; confirm with NBS which entry holds it) |
+| `tax_exemptions/...MoF-Q1.XLSX` | Ministry of Finance | **unclear, treated as no** (terms silent on the workbook; general prohibition of reproduction outside the copyright notice) | public page https://www.mof.go.tz/publications/tax-exemptions |
+| `worldbank/*.json` (from Block C1) | World Bank | **yes**, CC BY 4.0 (attribute the World Bank, WDI) | public API |
+
+## 3. How to cite (catalogue text, verbatim; see SOURCES.csv)
+
+* ILFS 2024: the catalogue field reads "National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) [Tanzania] 2022. Tanzania Integrated Labour Force Survey 2020/21, Dodoma, Tanzania: NBS". It names the 2020/21 round, not 2024: ask NBS which wording applies. Until then cite the published report as well: NBS (2025), *The Labour Market: Key Findings from the ILFS 2024*.
+* Census 2022: "National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) [Tanzania]2022 National Demographic Socio Economic Profile.Dodoma, Tanzania: NBS" (names a publication, not the microdata). The age counts are checked against NBS (2022), *The 2022 Population and Housing Census: Age and Sex Distribution Report*.
+* FinScope 2023: no citation requirement found; working wording "FinScope Tanzania 2023 (FSDT)", to be confirmed with FSDT. The existing acknowledgement text in `economic_model.json` (`finscope_acknowledgement`) stays.
+* MoF workbook: no requirement; cite title, publisher and the publication page.
+
+## 4. What this repository publishes and does not publish
+
+**Published (aggregates only)**: `data/processed/census_age_counts.json`, `data/processed/ilfs_indicators.json`, `data/processed/finscope_region_activity.json`, `data/processed/finscope_active_benchmark.json`, `data/interim/finscope_summary.json`, `data/interim/finscope_feature_store.json`, everything in `outputs/stats` and `outputs/tables`.
+
+**Not published**: everything under `data/raw/` except `SOURCES.csv` and READMEs (enforced by `.gitignore`; `git check-ignore` confirms the FinScope, ILFS, census and MoF files are ignored).
+
+**Synthetic, not derived from respondents**: `outputs/stats/finscope_targeting_population.json` (5,000 of 50,000 rows of a *synthetic* population from `economic_model.build_segmentation_model`; only the mobile-money penetration input is a real FinScope aggregate).
+
+## 5. Items the audit flagged (details in BLOCK_C_REPORT.md; nothing was deleted or changed)
+
+1. **Raw FinScope files are in git history and in HEAD.** `pipeline/FinScope.csv` (40,471,044 bytes) and `pipeline/FinScope Datamap.xlsx` were added in commit `1a78b61` (2026-07-23) and are still tracked at HEAD; the local `origin/main` equals HEAD, so they were probably pushed to `https://github.com/JascoJohn/TRA_Innovation_Jasco_John`. Whether that repository is public was not checked (no network lookups beyond the permitted sites). `.gitignore` does not untrack them. Remedy options (not applied; history rewriting is outside this block): make the repository private now, or rewrite history to drop the two blobs.
+2. **Small cells.** 42 of the 124 region x activity cells published in `finscope_region_activity.json` and `finscope_active_benchmark.json` rest on fewer than 10 respondents (35 on fewer than 8, minimum 1); 17 of 31 region TIN rates in `finscope_summary.json` rest on fewer than 10 TIN holders (one region has none). The dashboard refuses an estimate below 8 respondents but still shows cells with 8 or 9.
